# public/_headers — Cloudflare Pages
#
# frame-ancestors cannot be set from a <meta http-equiv> tag, so it has to arrive as an HTTP
# header (the site-wide `/*` block below). X-Frame-Options is the legacy fallback for older
# browsers.
#
# How rules combine (Cloudflare Pages docs, "Headers"): a request inherits the headers of EVERY
# rule whose pattern matches it, and a header set by two rules has its values joined with a
# comma. For Content-Security-Policy a comma separates two policies, and the browser enforces
# BOTH: policies intersect, they never widen each other. A narrower rule overlapping a practice
# prefix would silently narrow it. src/lib/engines/practice-policy.test.ts holds every rule here
# against every practice prefix and against every target the integrate workflows mirror.

# ——— The practices' surfaces: one shared policy ——————————————————————————————————————————
#
# 2026-10-05, Frank's decision (wording private): the machine-run practices may publish RICH
# works on this site — interactive and generative pieces, 3D/WebGL scenes, interactive video
# and sound, whole multi-page sites, built apps, WebAssembly (Pyodide among them) and live data
# from public APIs. Size and form are not limited. Every path a practice's own pages are served
# from bare carries the same policy, word for word, so no practice may do less than another
# and no new mirror can arrive with a narrower one:
#
#   script-src   'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' blob:
#                Scripts from FOREIGN HOSTS still do not run (Frank's decision of 2026-09-04
#                stands). A work vendors its libraries into its practice's repository, the
#                mirror brings them along, and they run from this origin. eval and WebAssembly
#                compilation, because three.js loaders, Pyodide and many built apps need them;
#                blob:, because workers and generated modules are made from blobs.
#   worker-src   'self' blob:
#   style-src    'self' 'unsafe-inline'            stylesheets and fonts are vendored, too
#   img-src      'self' data: blob: https:
#   font-src     'self' data:
#   media-src    'self' data: blob: https:        sound and moving image, streamed or not
#   connect-src  'self' https: wss:               live data from any public API or socket,
#                                                 as for the house's own pages since 2026-09-04
#   frame-src    https:
#   manifest-src 'self'
#
# What it replaces: from 2026-08-16 every practice prefix carried `connect-src 'self'` with no
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval', no workers, no blob: and no image or media from another host — the
# sandbox that kept the exfiltration channel closed after the 2026-07-21 lock. The decision of
# 2026-10-05 opens it on purpose: a practice's work may read the world while it runs, as the
# house's pages may. The policy text lives in src/lib/engines/practice-policy.ts; a test keeps
# every line below identical to it.

# The Atelier: standalone works (scripts/atelier/integrate.ts), its own window (2026-08-16, the
# n-1 model carried to the practices) and its v3 public artifacts (2026-08-30/31), each mirrored
# bare by atelier-integrate.yml.
/atelier/werke-html/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' blob:; worker-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; font-src 'self' data:; media-src 'self' data: blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https: wss:; frame-src https:; manifest-src 'self'

/atelier/window/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' blob:; worker-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; font-src 'self' data:; media-src 'self' data: blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https: wss:; frame-src https:; manifest-src 'self'

